# Test: ./dash --memcheck. Normal code leaves nothing alive; a struct stored in a
# list of Ints escapes (kept until exit), a String in a list of Strings does not; C code that frees twice or uses a freed object
# is reported. The summary is printed at exit.
#
# memcheck
# expect-c: _dash_tmp_release_f(0);
# expect-out: 6
# expect-out: 20
# expect-out: memcheck: ERROR objeto usado tras liberarse (en tests/test_memcheck.dash:60)
# expect-out: memcheck: ERROR objeto usado tras liberarse (en tests/test_memcheck.dash:60)
# expect-out: memcheck: ERROR release de un objeto sin referencias (en tests/test_memcheck.dash:60)
# expect-out: memcheck: ERROR string liberado dos veces (en tests/test_memcheck.dash:60)
# expect-out: fin
# expect-out: memcheck: vivos 1 objetos y 0 strings (escapados 1 y 0), errores 4

struct P
    x: Int
    y: Int
end

func f(n)
    a = [1, 2, n]
    p = P(n, 2)
    s = "v" + n
    return a[2] + p.x
end

@native func errores()
"""
    DashArrayLong *a = DashArray_create(2);
    STRPTR s = _dash_str_dup((STRPTR)"hola", FALSE);
    _Dash_P *p = _dash_struct_create_P(1, 2);
    _dash_retain(a);
    _dash_release(a);          /* freed here */
    _dash_retain(a);           /* used after being freed */
    _dash_retain(p);
    _dash_release(p);
    _dash_release(p);          /* freed, then released again: also "used after" */
    _dash_release(_dash_struct_create_P(3, 4));   /* a new temporary nobody retained */
    _dash_str_free(s);
    _dash_str_free(s);         /* freed twice */
"""
end

Main
    b = [1, 2]
    q = P(1, 2)
    t = "hola " + 3
    Print f(3)
    total = 0
    for i in (1..100)
        u = P(i, i)
        total = total + f(1) - u.x + i
    end
    Print total / 10
    lista = [0]
    lista[0] = P(5, 6)
    nombres = ["a"]
    nombres[0] = "x" + total
    errores()
    Print "fin"
end
